WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
The other development, I guess, would have been the technology.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:09.240
So we moved from reel-to-reel in the production room to SAW.

3
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:15.140
And SAW was this software that you could cut digital video with, and that was a huge transformation.

4
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.020
And at first I was like, “Oh I don’t know about this.”

5
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:25.160
It turned out to be an amazing thing because you can archive things so much easier, it takes up less space.

6
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.800
But it was a little weird to chop things up.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.640
Because I’m kind of coming at it where at WBRH, also, we were using a reel-to-reel, so I had been kind of invested in that technology.

8
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:43.680
And I felt very confident in my ability to cut the tape and to pattern things in a certain way and . . . You could control things with phasing,

9
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.640
and there were all these, like, cool tricks that I felt that I had mastered, you know.

10
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.240
It’s always kind of fun with production.

11
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.980
It’s so creative and . . . With the computer it was like anything was possible, but how do you do it?

12
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.940
And it was this whole, like, brand new era.
